<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<phpunit xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="vendor/phpunit/phpunit/phpunit.xsd"
         bootstrap="tests/bootstrap.php"
         colors="true"
>
    <!--
        The same suite, against MySQL/MariaDB instead of SQLite.

            vendor/bin/pest -c phpunit.mysql.xml

        ## Why this file exists

        phpunit.xml pins DB_CONNECTION=sqlite and DB_DATABASE=:memory:, which is
        right for the default suite: it is fast, needs no service, and runs
        anywhere. What it is not is the database ETHR ships on.

        The two drivers are not interchangeable, and the differences have
        already produced defects in this repository that a green SQLite run did
        not see:

          - MySQL DATE columns truncate the time component on insert; SQLite
            keeps it. A due_date carrying a time therefore made dunning fire a
            day late on SQLite and on time on MySQL.
          - PDO::quote() escapes newlines on MySQL and does not on SQLite, so a
            dump could tear on one driver and not the other. Every backup test
            in this repository ran on the driver where it tore.

        Both were found by looking, not by the suite. This file makes the
        question answerable by running it.

        ## Not a replacement for phpunit.xml

        This is slower, needs a running server, and is not wired into
        scripts/gates.sh. A gate that cannot run on a developer's machine
        without a service is a gate that gets skipped, and a skipped gate
        reports success. Run it deliberately: before a release, after touching
        anything that writes dates or raw SQL, and when a test behaves
        differently in production than it did locally.

        ## Setup

            CREATE DATABASE ethr_suite_mysql CHARACTER SET utf8mb4
                COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

        RefreshDatabase migrates this database on the first test and wraps every
        test in a transaction, so it is rebuilt rather than accumulated - but
        point it at a scratch database regardless: a test that issues DDL (see
        BackupRestoreRehearsalTest) cannot be rolled back on MySQL.

        ## Connection settings are overridable, and deliberately so

        DB_CONNECTION is forced - this file exists to pin the driver and would
        be pointless otherwise. The five settings that locate the server are
        NOT forced, so exporting DB_HOST / DB_PORT / DB_DATABASE / DB_USERNAME /
        DB_PASSWORD wins over the defaults below. That is what CI does: the
        workflow's service container issues credentials this file cannot know.

        (An earlier version of this file forced all of them while its own
        comment claimed they could be overridden. They could not.)
    -->
    <testsuites>
        <testsuite name="Unit">
            <directory>tests/Unit</directory>
        </testsuite>
        <testsuite name="Feature">
            <directory>tests/Feature</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <source>
        <include>
            <directory>app</directory>
        </include>
    </source>
    <php>
        <ini name="memory_limit" value="1G"/>
        <env name="APP_ENV" value="testing" force="true"/>
        <env name="APP_MAINTENANCE_DRIVER" value="file" force="true"/>
        <env name="BCRYPT_ROUNDS" value="4" force="true"/>
        <env name="BROADCAST_CONNECTION" value="null" force="true"/>
        <env name="CACHE_STORE" value="array" force="true"/>

        <!-- The only lines that differ from phpunit.xml. -->
        <env name="DB_CONNECTION" value="mariadb" force="true"/>
        <!-- Not forced: the environment wins. See the header. -->
        <env name="DB_HOST" value="127.0.0.1"/>
        <env name="DB_PORT" value="3306"/>
        <env name="DB_DATABASE" value="ethr_suite_mysql"/>
        <env name="DB_USERNAME" value="root"/>
        <env name="DB_PASSWORD" value=""/>
        <env name="DB_URL" value="" force="true"/>

        <env name="FILESYSTEM_DISK" value="minio" force="true"/>
        <env name="MAIL_MAILER" value="array" force="true"/>
        <env name="QUEUE_CONNECTION" value="sync" force="true"/>
        <env name="SESSION_DRIVER" value="array" force="true"/>
        <env name="PULSE_ENABLED" value="false" force="true"/>
        <env name="TELESCOPE_ENABLED" value="false" force="true"/>
        <env name="NIGHTWATCH_ENABLED" value="false" force="true"/>
    </php>
</phpunit>
